schema: claim-evidence
object:
  title: Bank/wire cross-border transfers can lose 6%+ to fees vs. crypto
  type: claim-evidence
  claim: >-
    Sending money internationally through banks or services like Western
    Union can lose 6% or more to fees, and small grassroots projects often
    can't easily open accounts, whereas crypto can move value to a wallet in
    minutes for a much smaller cost.
  evidence: >-
    Stated in how-to-get-crypto.md's "Why this might actually matter for
    your work" section as the article's core cross-border-cost rationale for
    considering crypto at all.
  source_lineage: src/content/docs/how-to-get-crypto.md
  interpretation: >-
    Used to justify why a grassroots/community organization might adopt
    crypto for receiving grants or donations despite the article's own
    scam-risk warnings.
  uncertainty: >-
    The "6% or more" figure and "much smaller cost" framing are asserted
    without a cited source, exact fee comparison, or date; remittance and
    on/off-ramp fees vary significantly by corridor, amount, and provider.
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/how-to-get-crypto.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted
